Trusted package-signing keys.

Every `*.pub` in this directory is a key this machine will accept a signature
from — for the binhost index (PACKAGES.sig) and for a package's own `.sig`
sidecar. Adding a key is copying a file in; removing trust is deleting one.
There is no revocation list and no online check: the directory IS the policy.

    kpkg keygen builder          # on the machine that builds
    cp builder.pub /etc/kdos/keys/   # on every machine that should trust it

A key id (16 hex characters, printed by kpkg) identifies a key. It is NOT a
credential: a signature file names the id so a person can be told which key
signed, and verification always uses the key from THIS directory.

KDOS ships no key here. A distro that shipped its own trusted key in the image
would be asking you to trust whoever built the image, which is exactly the
question signing exists to let you answer for yourself.
